{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1180266-curses-hexes-and-other-foul-magicks","id":1180266,"title":"Curses, Hexes, and other foul magicks.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-28T15:27:00-08:00","id":1180266,"title":"Curses, Hexes, and other foul magicks.","content":"Imagine if you would, an Autumn Courtier that has dedicated the majority of his time and efforts towards researching, cataloguing and inventing any magic that could be used to bring low the enemies of the freehold. What sort of curses could he discover or create in this endeavor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:09:44-08:00","id":1180317,"title":"","content":"Are we talking strictly within the realm of Changeling, or with the potential aid of other kinds of supernaturals? As far as Changeling magic goes, one of the ultimate playing field levelers was a goblin contract called Blood Binding. It could more or less prevent a True Fae from being able to use its contracts, making the odds of overwhelming it with force and numbers much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T20:45:14-08:00","id":1180333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1180266-curses-hexes-and-other-foul-magicks?p=1180317#post1180317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we talking strictly within the realm of Changeling, or with the potential aid of other kinds of supernaturals? As far as Changeling magic goes, one of the ultimate playing field levelers was a goblin contract called Blood Binding. It could more or less prevent a True Fae from being able to use its contracts, making the odds of overwhelming it with force and numbers much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything goes, so long as it\u2019s magical in origin and is designed to subtly hinder or incapacitate it\u2019s target. I\u2019ll even accept various homebrew works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:19:37-08:00","id":1180338,"title":"","content":"Mages have Fate spells, but any Arcana could be used to \u201ccurse\u201d people when given the right spin. Although Fate is often most subtle one. Mages can Imbue objects with such spells and lend it to changelings, or changelings can pick up an Artifact or two. <br /> <br /> Beasts have their Nightmares. I can\u2019t recall if there was a way for non-Beasts to use them, though. <br /> <br /> Some werewolf Gifts and Rites that hamper and harry the prey work well as curses. Talens and fetishes can contain Gift Facets or Gift-like powers, and changelings in a pack could participate in Pack Rites. (Haven\u2019t yet read The Pack, so not sure on such extended packs)<br /> <br /> Vampiric Disciplines and Devotions, including Theban Sorcery and Cr\u00faac, all so fit the black magic theme. Especially with Nghtmare and Nightmare-based Devotions, and Cr\u00faac rituals. But as with Beast Nightmares, I don\u2019t know if there\u2019s a way for changelings to use them. <br /> <br /> Geist 1E had various types of objects that houses ghostly power, so you could mine it for ideas, but I have no idea how they\u2019ll do it in 2E. <br /> <br /> Demonic Embeds and Exploits can manifest as \u201ctraditional\u201d demonic phenomena (as much as I hate that sort of description), despite the book and some fans &amp; critics overly emphasizing the surreal techno-occult aesthetics of Demon. A changeling can get hold of gadgets fhat contain Embeds and/or Exploits of varying power and subtlety. <br /> <br /> EDIT: My lore on Mummy is fuzzy and inadequate, but Relics are wonderful ways to curse people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:31:50-08:00","id":1180341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1180266-curses-hexes-and-other-foul-magicks?p=1180338#post1180338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have Fate spells, but any Arcana could be used to \u201ccurse\u201d people when given the right spin. Although Fate is often most subtle one. Mages can Imbue objects with such spells and lend it to changelings, or changelings can pick up an Artifact or two. <br /> <br /> Beasts have their Nightmares. I can\u2019t recall if there was a way for non-Beasts to use them, though. <br /> <br /> Some werewolf Gifts and Rites that hamper and harry the prey work well as curses. Talens and fetishes can contain Gift Facets or Gift-like powers, and changelings in a pack could participate in Pack Rites. (Haven\u2019t yet read The Pack, so not sure on such extended packs)<br /> <br /> Vampiric Disciplines and Devotions, including Theban Sorcery and Cr\u00faac, all so fit the black magic theme. Especially with Nghtmare and Nightmare-based Devotions, and Cr\u00faac rituals. But as with Beast Nightmares, I don\u2019t know if there\u2019s a way for changelings to use them. <br /> <br /> Geist 1E had various types of objects that houses ghostly power, so you could mine it for ideas, but I have no idea how they\u2019ll do it in 2E. <br /> <br /> Demonic Embeds and Exploits can manifest as \u201ctraditional\u201d demonic phenomena (as much as I hate that sort of description), despite the book and some fans &amp; critics overly emphasizing the surreal techno-occult aesthetics of Demon. A changeling can get hold of gadgets fhat contain Embeds and/or Exploits of varying power and subtlety. <br /> <br /> EDIT: My lore on Mummy is fuzzy and inadequate, but Relics are wonderful ways to curse people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas, but the problem is that Changelings are paranoid as fuck by their nature and probably wouldn\u2019t trust any non-changeling any further than they could throw them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23780-overlord62","name":"Overlord62","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T21:38:28-08:00","id":1180342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overlord62</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1180266-curses-hexes-and-other-foul-magicks?p=1180341#post1180341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting ideas, but the problem is that Changelings are paranoid as fuck by their nature and probably wouldn\u2019t trust any non-changeling any further than they could throw them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then maybe all those toys were stolen or taken as trophies? Or maybe the changelings managed to successfully ensnare the others in supernatural bargains since they\u2019re good at that. <br /> <br /> Either way, inviting out-of-context magic is indeed risky, but it can certainly throw Huntsmen and hobgoblins off their guard (and perhaps even the Gentry themselves).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}